SUMMARY:[Remembrance Ceremony · West Kelowna] Remembrance Day: West Kelown
 a (Legion Branch #288)
DESCRIPTION:WHEN: Wednesday\, November 11\, 2026\, 10:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m.
  (Kelowna time)\nWHERE: Royal LePage Place\, 2760 Cameron Rd\, West Kelown
 a\, BC\n\nCATEGORY: Ceremonies & Commemorations\nTYPE: Remembrance Ceremon
 y\nJURISDICTION: West Kelowna\nFEDERAL RIDING: Okanagan Lake West—South 
 Kelowna\nTAGS: Open to Public\, Free\, Mayor & Council\, MP\, Veterans\, D
 etails TBC\n\nABOUT:\nHosted by Royal Canadian Legion Westbank Branch #288
 . The 2026 listing says to be seated by 10:30 a.m.\; the service starts at
  10:45\, with the moment of silence at 11 and the service ending around no
 on. In past years an honour parade stepped off around 10 a.m. (parade time
  not confirmed for 2026). The MP and local councils usually attend.\n\nWHY
  IT MATTERS (GOVERNMENT RELATIONS):\nThe main Remembrance Day ceremony in 
 Dan Albas's riding.\n\nDETAILS:\nOrganizer: Royal Canadian Legion Westbank
  Branch #288\nWho attends: Veterans\, MP Dan Albas (usually)\, West Kelown
 a council\, WFN representatives\, residents\nCost: Free\nAccess: Open to t
 he public\; be seated by 10:30 a.m.\n\nNOT YET CONFIRMED: Parade time for 
 2026.\n\nSOURCE: https://www.valleyvibe.ca/events/remembrance-day-kelowna-
 2026
LOCATION:Royal LePage Place\, 2760 Cameron Rd\, West Kelowna\, BC
CATEGORIES:Ceremonies & Commemorations,Remembrance Ceremony,West Kelowna,Op
 en to Public,Free,Mayor & Council,MP,Veterans,Details TBC
